# Security

## Authentication

- **Frontend:** Supabase Auth via `@supabase/ssr` httpOnly cookies; session refresh in `lib/supabase/proxy.ts`.
- **Backend:** Bearer JWT verified via Supabase JWKS (ES256/RS256); `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET` only as legacy HS256 fallback.
- Use `CurrentUser` on protected routes — do not reimplement JWT parsing.

## Authorization (RLS)

| Resource | Rule |
|----------|------|
| `forms` | Owner CRUD; anon blocked |
| `public_forms` view | anon `SELECT` for published rows only |
| `form_responses` | anon `INSERT` only if parent form `status = 'published'`; owner `SELECT`/`DELETE` |
| `storage.objects` (`sketches`) | First path segment must equal `auth.uid()` |

**Never** loosen `forms` RLS for public access — extend `public_forms` instead.

## Service role (critical)

`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`:

- ✅ Backend read of `sketches` bucket (no user read policy for service)
- ✅ Server-side ops that intentionally bypass RLS (rare; document why)
- ❌ Browser, Client Components, or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- ❌ Table writes from backend — use `get_user_client(jwt)` so RLS applies

Defense in depth: `_ensure_path_owned_by` in `routers/forms.py` before queueing generate jobs (storage download bypasses RLS).

## Public form surface (`/f/[slug]`)

- Expose only `public_slug` — never internal `forms.id` in UI or URLs.
- Slug is `nanoid(12)` — unguessable; assign at publish.
- Validate submissions server-side against `definition` (field IDs, types, required).

## Input validation

- **Frontend:** Zod / shared validators before insert.
- **Backend:** Pydantic models (`Definition`, API payloads); `/forms/validate` for editor saves.
- **Uploads:** MIME `image/jpeg|png|webp`, 10 MB cap, correct storage path layout.

## Secrets & environment

| File | Contains |
|------|----------|
| Root `.env` | Shared Supabase keys (dev) |
| `frontend/.env.local` | `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` + server keys for Next |
| `backend/.env` | See `backend/.env.example` |

Never commit real keys. Never log JWTs, service role key, or LLM API keys.

## API

- CORS from `CORS_ORIGINS` in backend settings (JSON list).
- CORS misconfiguration is a deployment risk — keep origins explicit.
- Error responses: safe messages to clients; stack traces in server logs only.

## Dependencies

- Lockfiles: `frontend/package-lock.json`, `backend/uv.lock`.
- Run `npm audit` / review advisories before releases.

## Pre-merge security checklist

- [ ] No secrets in diff
- [ ] RLS policies unchanged or tightened (not bypassed)
- [ ] `public_forms` updated if new respondent-visible columns
- [ ] Service role not introduced to frontend
- [ ] New public routes added to `proxy.ts` public paths if needed
